{"kind":"text","seq":34,"text":"My best score this round is **6.95 excitement** (intensity 10.21, nausea 6.03). It's only a small gain over last round's 6.94, and intensity is still just over the ~10 target.\n\n**Winning build:** a taller version of last round's layout. It's 76 pieces with a 17-segment chain lift, a highest drop of 34 (up from 26), six inversions (three vertical loops and four corkscrews), booster-driven airtime hills, and a speed-18 brake at the bottom of the first drop so the train doesn't hit the first loop too fast. Similarity to the stock designs is 0.36 (nearest is Time Twister), below the 0.5 penalty limit.\n\n**What the other runs showed:**\n- **Taller lift with no brake:** intensity jumped to 15.3 and excitement fell to 1.61, because the first loop was taken too fast. The speed-18 brake fixed this.\n- **Lower booster and brake speeds:** intensity dropped slightly but so did excitement (6.87–6.94). The lowest setting (first brake at 16) made the test fail to complete, most likely because the train stalled.\n- **Banked turn at the top of the lift:** 6.90, and max lateral G stayed at 2.89. So the unbanked turn at the top isn't what causes the high sideways forces; it's more likely the corkscrews.\n\nThese tweaks have hit a ceiling around 6.9, so beating it in a later round will need a different layout, not more speed changes."}
